# Rule: Client arcs (/arcs)

Mirror of [`.claude/rules/arcs.md`](../../.claude/rules/arcs.md) — read
that file; it is the canonical text. Read first: ADR-052 (the deck
chassis), ADR-057 (terminal motion), ADR-072 (the portfolio arc, the
`dossier` section kind, the shared evidence, the envelope on arcs), ADR-073
(the site's header on every arc; the left reel deleted), ADR-090 (the
dossier is one housing — proposed), ADR-098 (clients, the overview's
filter, the `configuration` kind, the scaffold — proposed).

⚠ ADR-098: an `ArcDef` gains `client` / `kind` / `theme`, and `/arcs/<client>`
lists that client's engagements INSIDE the existing `[slug]` route — the two
slug sets share a namespace and are pinned disjoint. NO URL MOVED: engagements
stay flat, because an arc's whole distribution is a link somebody forwarded.
`kind` is DERIVED from `format` where it can be, so no pre-existing content
module was edited; `format` stays the LAYOUT family (a portfolio and a
proposal are both productions and lay out alike). The overview groups by
client and filters by kind, writing ONE attribute with the narrowing in CSS
over server-rendered `data-kind` / `data-kinds` — no `:has()`, and no
attribute means everything is shown. The `configuration` kind is ADR-052's
SECOND exception to "content-only" after the dossier: one client leaf, one
delegated listener, the resting state authored, `data-cfg-*` never
`data-arc-*`, and the pitch page's grammar COPIED onto the ADR-077 ramp
rather than shared. A `theme: "light"` arc is two halves — the mount and a
hand-written `LIGHT_LOCKED_ROUTES` row. `scripts/new-arc.mjs` scaffolds a
client page in one command and ships finished copy, never placeholders.

⚠ ADR-118: `/arcs` is the owner's page (ADR-117) and an INSTRUMENT — a
monitor that plots every engagement at its filing date, then a log that opens
it (contracts in `.cursor/rules/sheet.mdc`). Every `ArcDef` and
`ClientPageDef` carries `date` (YYYY-MM-DD, OWNER-TO-CONFIRM), reversing
ADR-098's no-date ruling on its own terms: it feeds a plot, and
`arcs-registry` checks each client's registry order against it. A `-v2` cut
authors its own `date:` line; the scaffold takes `--date`. Since ADR-118 U2
the log's dossier DRAWS each proposal's configuration from its own
`configuration` section — an edit to a workstream's `where` / `runs` prose
moves a chip, and `sheet-config-fit` pins each reading by name.

⚠ ADR-098 U1: the journey row in the top-left corner is hidden on EVERY
surface now — the arcs asked, then the homepage, so the rule and the bracket's
return live in `rail-instruments.css` (the ≤960 rung promoted to every width)
and the route-scoped copies in `arcs.css` and `trinny-london.css` are deleted.
Do not re-add one. `display: none`, never unmounted, so the rosters stay
exercised. Unlike the pitch page an arc KEEPS its section indicator: the
header is the site's own. And a
PROPOSAL's interstitial line drops to `clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 40px)` at 42ch,
scoped to the format — a deck is presented in a room, a proposal is read at
arm's length.

⚠ ADR-090: the four dossier beats are one machined housing (ADR-089's
grammar at page scale) with the console as a square CELL inside it, all
`.arc-dossier`-scoped and gated at `(min-width: 981px) and
(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`. Three traps, all measured: the
ADR-052 reveal's `rootMargin: -10%` is a DEAD BAND the housing may not fill
into (`--dos-reveal-clear`; the cost is double the clearance, and it binds
only at tall viewports where the console sets the row); `.arc-head` carries
`.arc-reveal`, whose transform is the containing block, so the header
band's seat is declared rather than inherited; and the housing's inset is
paid for by the FIELD, where `.fl-bay__top` is already clipped. The housing
also makes `--arc-plate` the record column's BED in light — a new text rung
there belongs in the contrast walk.

⚠ ADR-098 U4 + U5 (owner, 2026-09-14): the three `plates` groups are a
NOTCHED HOUSING — TOP-RIGHT, and only top-right. The plate's floor IS the
inverse DELIVERABLE band and its text is set inside it, so a bottom-left
chamfer bites the line the reader is on; a cut is free only where nothing is
set against it. One corner is lawful by ADR-065's uniform-SET clause (three
plates, one nesting level, one scale, the LAWFUL diagonal's top end) and a
single notch MEANS oriented, which a numbered sequence is. NO `border` — a
clip cuts a border and never strokes one — so the edge is a two-contour
`evenodd` ring, inner leg `ch - 0.586px`. ⚠ The corner is pinned from BOTH
ends by HIT TEST, never by parsing the computed `clip-path` (which keeps its
percentages and `calc()`s), and the cut resolves through a probe element:
a custom property is a string until something lays it out. CSS-only, three
pages.

⚠ ADR-101 §B (owner, same day): THE PLATE'S FOOT IS NO LONGER INVERSE. Its
head band AND its foot both paint `--arc-gold-wash` — the BOARD CHIP's own
material, aliased from one token on `.arc-root` so the two cannot drift — with
the 2px `--gold-line` rule across the head stopping at the cut. On
`/arcs/trinny-london/proposal` that chip literally travels here and lands as
this band, and the owner ruled out a cross-fade; the answer is that there is
only one material. ⚠ The RING becomes visible over the foot, and that is the
point: U2 relied on the inverse band bleeding to the silhouette to CAP the
plate. Measured in light, head and foot composite to the identical
`rgb(223,208,180)` with `--gold-ink` at 4.81:1; DARK is defined by the ramp
and unverified, since every proposal route is light-locked.

⚠ ADR-100: the `board` kind is the FOURTH enumerated exception — the client's
configuration as a circuit board in two states (dormant beside lit), the
proof's R4 grammar at page scale, no frame, one leaf with no picker, SERVER-ONLY.
⚠ U2 (owner, 2026-09-14) is the live drawing: ONE RECORD of four facts (who
owns it · the context · the work · the tools) drawn TWICE — a ruled LEDGER on
the dormant side (four rows, a key and a value, hairlines, no housing and no
colour) beside the assembled BOARD (green seat + drop, THE CONTEXT's four
tags, the gold CHIP `AI CAPABILITY` / "owned by the team", four tools as
peers, three ribbons). The two sides may NOT mirror each other. No diamonds.
Both share the datum and the floor. ⚠ U1's ruling stands under it: when he
asks for simple, the FIRST cut is the minimal one.
⚠ U3 (same day, owner): the LEDGER arrives SLOWER — 0.72s at a 140ms stagger
against the board's 0.42/80 — because the board assembles in one gesture and
the ledger is four rows read in order. ⚠ EVERY LIT RUNG IS SCOPED
`[data-board-state="configured"]` or the whole ladder is DEAD: the rules that
start the animations are four classes, a bare `.arc-board.is-in
[data-board-role="card"]` is three, and `animation:` RESETS `animation-delay`
to zero. It shipped that way in U1 — a delay that does not apply fails
silently and reads as a taste decision. The smoke pins both ladders. Dispatched in BOTH `ArcSectionRenderer` and the
Trinny page's `TrinnyBeats` switch (which dropped `configuration`;
`ArcConfiguration` is byte-identical elsewhere). The row is width-led and its
shares are the crops' (560 + 40 + 800 = 1400; the flex bases and the seam are
pinned by `arc-board-fit`; the svg sits at its own height, no cap, no aspect);
every colour is an `--arc-board-*` alias of the ramp, never a `--pda-*`; every
dormant rule sits under `.is-arc-js` + `no-preference` so no-JS and PRM render
lit; `data-board-*` never `data-arc-*`; the head on the TEXT band, the drawing
on the INSTRUMENT band.

⚠ ADR-103 (2026-09-15): the `steps` kind is the FIFTH enumerated exception —
`{ head, items: [{ id, kicker, name, body, visual }] }`, `ArcSteps` SERVER-ONLY
with `data-steps-*` only, the deliverables as a stepped list of `.arc-plate`
rows (head band + a body line — the plates' own material, so on the Trinny
page the phase plates' bands travel to BECOME them) beside a stage per item.
⚠ EVERY MOTION CHANNEL IS A CUSTOM PROPERTY WITH A FINISHED DEFAULT
(`--tl-row-h`, `--tl-lit`, `--tl-vis`, `--scan-s`): the static render, no-JS
and PRM read every row open and filled, every stage shown, the scan complete;
a route scrubs them. A `visual` is `scan` (`ArcScanVisual`: a framed 4:5 field
on its own opaque bed, a gold edge sweeping the packshot over its grey ghost,
callouts as 7×7 nodes + 1px div leaders + labels, a verdict; no digits, no
svg, no opacity, no transition) or `field` (the frame with one centred node
over a designation). `trinny-offer` pins that no row restates a phase
("not a simulacrum of those three modules"). Canonical text:
`.claude/rules/arcs.md` §The client model; the record is ADR-103.

⚠ ADR-128 (2026-09-26, Proposed): `/arcs/pandora-proposal` is a FLAT arc in
ADR-126's proof register (films · a head over the `heimdall` dossier · sheets ·
intelligence), the first registered `board` (its tools row is ONE composed
line — three products, never an abbreviation), a day-rate ledger from one
constant; `arc-board-fit` walks every registered board and `sheet-instrument`
reads the real overview on `REAL_TODAY`. Phase B adds `proof-card` and `bench`
as the sixth and seventh exceptions. Canonical text: `.claude/rules/arcs.md`
§The client model.

Contracts in one breath: one scroll writer (`useArcScroll`); `--hero-lift`
gates the rails; the slice API is read-only; every section opaque void; no
three.js / Supabase / `LandingPage` imports — the casefile's dossier LEAVES
(`ToolField`, `MediaLightbox`, `ConsoleFrame`, `wireframes/**`,
`toolCardData`) are the one sanctioned import; page CSS lives in `arcs.css`
under `.arc-*`, with the casefile's `casefile.css` + `console.css` imported
at the ROUTE ahead of it and `theme.css` last; no italics; content changes
= `lib/arcs/content/*` + the registry; shared Loop evidence is imported by
reference from `content/shared/*`; the numbers canon fails on every arc;
the confidentiality envelope runs over the portfolio (the keynote deck
keeps its € rows — recorded); a dossier beat must FIT at 1280×720 /
1440×800 / 1920×1080; a bay change is a two-surface change (run the ring
smoke AND the portfolio smoke); the header is `ArcHudNav` (the landing's
`.hud__nav*` chrome — chapter links in the hero, the readout + drawer once
scrolled) and `ArcMenu` is deleted, with `menuPrimary` marking a chapter.
